  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safe Migration/CTIP Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Tajikistan):  The Safe Migration/CTIP Activity seeks to advance the safe migration and address trafficking in persons by reducing vulnerabilities to trafficking in persons (TIP) and protecting the dignity and human rights of Tajik  migrant laborers and other at-risk groups. The activity will attain the set objectives through prevention of TIP, protection of trafficking survivors, and partnerships with relevant stakeholders such as the Government of Tajikistan, civil society, and private sector.  The activity will attain the set objectives through prevention of TIP, protection of trafficking survivors, and improved partnerships with relevant stakeholders such as the Government of Tajikistan, civil society, and private sector.  More specifically, prevention components will  assist potential migrants and at-risk groups to make safe and informed migration decisions on the basis of accurate and reliable information; the protection pillar will engage with the national actors within the victim protection system to improve and expand their capacity to systematically protect victims of TIP; and finally, the partnership component will enhance more-relevant cooperation and partnership mechanisms and strategies for providing support to the trafficking survivors and preventing TIP. Furthermore, the Activity will support localizations in line with the New Partnership Initiative with 30-50% of the funds under this activity being made available to administer sub-awards to qualified local organizations for implementation of activities.Furthermore, the Activity will support localizations in line with the New Partnership Initiative with 30-50% of the funds under this activity being made available to administer sub-awards to qualified local organizations for implementation of activities..</narrative>
  </description>
